  "problem": "If $X={\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{7}},$ then $P(X)=$",
  "worked_solution": "The power set of $X,$ denoted $P(X),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $X,$ including the empty set $\u2205.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $X$ using a tree diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14095809/assets/04cf4a4f2113771f5aa5f948f1c460e1c4611dd1d0448dea50bbb5a8ecb32739.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $X$ are\n\n$$\n\u2205={},\\,{\\sqrt{5}},\\,{\\sqrt{7}},\\,{\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{7}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(X)={\u2205,{\\sqrt{5}},{\\sqrt{7}},{\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{7}}}.\n$$",
